{"type":"npc","name":"Unbound Arboreal","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":320,"temp":0,"max":320,"details":""},"ac":{"value":36,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"axe-vulnerability","value":10,"exceptions":[]},{"type":"fire","value":15,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"bludgeoning","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"piercing","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["arboreal","common","fey"],"details":"Speak with plants"},"level":{"value":15},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Deep within old-growth forests, ancient arboreals can spend countless cycles meditating on the changes each season brings, eventually absorbing the essence of this natural cycle into their bodies. Unlike arboreal archives, who actively focus on accumulating knowledge, unbound arboreals prefer to hone their understanding of the world through self-reflection, a difference in philosophy that leads to impassioned debates that can last for decades.</p><h2>Seasonal Variation</h2><p>Arboreals living in areas without four seasons might have different abilities than those described here. For example, an unbound arboreal in an equatorial region might have powers like Spring's Blossoming and Summer's Tangle during the rainy season. In the dry season, they could have a power similar to Autumn's Abscission and the ability to dry out nearby creatures.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 810/1,850/3,400 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics, Diplomacy, Lore [Forest], Nature, Occultism, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (vitality), ice, life, lifeward armor, mirrored, sensory (low-light vision), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.XkDCzMIyc0YOjw05]{Control Weather}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.qvwIwJ9QBihy8R0t]{Speak with Plants}), strength, sturdy, tangle shield, time, wild, wisdom, wood</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Aoife Ester","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":8},"dex":{"mod":-1},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":5},"wis":{"mod":8},"cha":{"mod":5}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":28,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":31,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":30,"special":[]},"diplomacy":{"base":28,"special":[]},"nature":{"base":33,"special":[]},"occultism":{"base":30,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":18,"special":[{"label":"in forests","predicate":["terrain:forest"],"base":28}]}},"traits":{"value":["plant","wood"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"nlYfiMrcHJbJ1vbp","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/unbound-arboreal.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Unbound Arboreal","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":3,"height":3,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/unbound-arboreal.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/unbound-arboreal.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"name":"Forest Lore","type":"lore","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"mod":{"value":30},"proficient":{"value":0}},"effects":[],"_id":"nRKPSyUvBcWp0yOk","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/lore.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Constant Spells","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","description":{"value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ConstantSpells]</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"constant-spells","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.kakyXBG5WA8c6Zfd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"O8k231EgRy2cbm54"},{"folder":"6JF73zNhT8zbp1qC","img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolts-salvo-clouds-sky.webp","name":"Control Weather (Doesn't Require a Secondary Caster)","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Area</strong> 2-mile-radius circle centered on you</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You alter the weather, making it calm and normal for the season or choosing up to two effects based on the season.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Spring</strong> drizzle, heat, hurricane, sleet, thunderstorm, tornado</li>\n<li><strong>Summer</strong> drizzle, downpour, extreme heat, hail, heat</li>\n<li><strong>Autumn</strong> cold weather, fog, mild heat, sleet</li>\n<li><strong>Winter</strong> blizzard, mild cold, extreme cold, thaw</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can't specifically control the manifestations, such as the exact path of a tornado or the targets of lightning strikes.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> You change the weather as desired and can affect a larger area (up to a 5-mile-radius circle), or a longer duration (any number of additional d12 hours, up to 16d12).</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> You change the weather as desired.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> You fail to change the weather as desired.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The weather changes in an unanticipated way, determined by the GM but generally as contradictory to your true desires as possible (for instance, a terrible storm emerges when you would prefer good weather).</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (9th)</strong> You can create unseasonable weather and contradictory weather effects, such as extreme cold and a hurricane. You can make the weather calm and normal weather for a different season or choose weather effects from any season's list.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"control-weather","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"uncommon","traditions":[]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":8},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":null,"time":{"value":"1 day"},"duration":{"value":"4d12 hours","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":null},"counteraction":false,"ritual":{"primary":{"check":"Nature (master)"},"secondary":{"casters":1,"checks":"Survival"}}},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.XkDCzMIyc0YOjw05","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"nm5LUhWqtu8boi7j"},{"name":"Primal Innate Spells","type":"spellcastingEntry","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"ability":{"value":"cha"},"spelldc":{"value":28,"dc":36},"tradition":{"value":"primal"},"prepared":{"value":"innate"},"showSlotlessLevels":{"value":false},"proficiency":{"value":1},"slots":{"slot0":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot1":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot2":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot3":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot4":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot5":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot6":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot7":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot8":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot9":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot10":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot11":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0}},"autoHeightenLevel":{"value":null}},"_id":"GEC81X0gRx4RqOam","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/spellcastingEntry.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"folder":"4fJHnYFqH0VjZXPv","img":"icons/magic/nature/plant-poison-spit-green.webp","name":"Speak with Plants (At Will)","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You can ask questions of and receive answers from plants and fungi, but the spell doesn't make them more friendly or intelligent than normal. Most normal plants and fungi have a distinctive view of the world around them, so they don't recognize details about creatures or know anything about the world beyond their immediate vicinity. Cunning plant or fungus monsters are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (4th)</strong> The duration is 8 hours.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"speak-with-plants","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","plant","wood"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["divine","occult","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 hour","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"GEC81X0gRx4RqOam"},"counteraction":false},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.qvwIwJ9QBihy8R0t","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"YIkP9lEym7MrL1c1"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","description":{"value":"","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","predicate":["item:magical"],"selector":"saving-throw","type":"status","value":1}],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"1-status-to-all-saves-vs-magic","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.kquBnQ0kObZztnBc","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"cCV2iaJPFiqSuOEV"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/FreeAction.webp","name":"Improved Pull 50 Feet","system":{"actionType":{"value":"free"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unbound arboreal hits with their boundless root Strike</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal uses Pull.</p><hr /><p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Pull]</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"pull","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null},"deathNote":false},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.BYF0XL1ZtdkRda3u","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"QxwK2QXLM265ex3T"},{"type":"melee","name":"Branch","effects":[],"system":{"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null},"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["agile","reach-15"]},"damageRolls":{"SII7MXBYpfyy924n":{"damage":"3d10+14","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":30},"attackEffects":{"value":[]}},"_id":"12UAixLGuaMMXltt","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"melee","name":"Boundless Root","effects":[],"system":{"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null},"description":{"value":"","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["reach-200"]},"damageRolls":{"BDgu81DjJQJnkJk7":{"damage":"3d6+14","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":"persistent"}},"bonus":{"value":30},"attackEffects":{"value":["pull"]}},"_id":"zSWeHzDGYjF4xskJ","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"False Felling","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per day</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unbound arboreal is reduced to 0 Hit Points, and their wounded value is 2 or less</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal's trunk splits, crashing down on their foes before rewinding time to remain standing. All creatures in a @Template[type:line|distance:20] take @Damage[6d8[bludgeoning]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:33|basic] save). The arboreal avoids being knocked @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious} and remains at 1 Hit Point, but their wounded value increases by 1.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":true,"frequency":{"max":1,"per":"day","value":1}},"effects":[],"_id":"qTrm5uHMcvTVHPJC","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Stumbling Roots","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature attempts to uses an action with the move trait to exit a square within 15 feet of the unbound arboreal</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal raises the base of one of their roots out of the ground, attempting to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.ge56Lu1xXVFYUnLP]{Trip} the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the unbound arboreal's multiple attack penalty.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"pRSaQD0JRgfpV45g","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Autumn's Abscission","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by autumn</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal unleashes a shower of razor-sharp leaves, dealing @Damage[8d6[slashing]|options:area-damage] damage to all creatures in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:15] (@Check[reflex|dc:36|basic] save).</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":2},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"hDn96o7fmEQDFKoA","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Spring's Blossoming","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by spring</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal draws on spring's new growth, shedding healing petals. The unbound arboreal and all living creatures of the arboreal's choice in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:15] recover @Damage[6d8[healing]|options:area-damage] Hit Points, and all undead creatures within 15 feet take @Damage[6d8[vitality]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[fortitude|dc:36|basic] save).</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["healing","primal","vitality"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":2},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"B47Yv4RXetxzuGmd","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Summer's Tangle","system":{"actionType":{"value":"free"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by summer</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal spreads summer's wild growth, causing all squares in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:15] to become greater difficult terrain until the start of their next turn. The unbound arboreal is not impeded by this growth. In addition, a creature that ends its turn in an affected space must succeed at a @Check[reflex|dc:33] save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.kWc1fhmv9LBiTuei]{Grabbed} by the unbound arboreal until the end of that creature's next turn ([[/act escape dc=33]]).</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["plant","primal"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false,"frequency":{"max":1,"per":"round"}},"effects":[],"_id":"ZeAbVaDKaycwUGgF","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Winter's Withering","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by winter</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal invokes the withering chill of winter, enervating those in their vicinity. Each creature in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:15] takes @Damage[10d6[cold]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[fortitude|dc:36|basic] save); creatures that fail additionally become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} for 1 round, or for 1 minute on a critical failure.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["cold","primal"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":3},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"NzweO6Ktvw4VQA1I","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Confluence of Seasons","system":{"actionType":{"value":"free"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unbound arboreal's turn begins</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal can control their passage through the cycle of seasons if they don't want to remain in their current season. The arboreal becomes influenced by either the previous season in the cycle or the next. The influencing season determines which abilities they can use. An unbound arboreal typically begins an encounter influenced by the current season.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"ywtEyHWIhDKoAqmG","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}}],"effects":[],"sort":400000,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.8.0"}}